    Implement TLS proxy agent with token-based authorization
    
    - Add runTlsProxy() — a TCP server that accepts TLS connections on
      a given port using OpenSSL.
    - Each client connection is handled in a separate std::thread to
      allow concurrent sessions.
    - On handshake, the client must send a token in the format
      "TOKEN: <hex>\n"; verification uses a hash loaded from a file
      (token generated by a separate module).
    - After successful authorization, the proxy relays traffic between
      the client and the internal backend (api-gateway) without
      encryption on the local side; two parallel threads are used for
      bidirectional data forwarding (relayLoop).
    - Add helper functions: listening socket creation, backend
      connection, line reading from TLS, relay loop.
    - Use raw POSIX sockets and OpenSSL for TLS; configuration
      (ports, certificate/key paths) is passed via TlsProxyConfig.

